\title{2.3 The executable: shares, instructions and hardware events of the loader thread}

\p{49,155 samples of the loader thread in two profiled passes of the symbolised base image (24.6 s). Per pass: \strong{147 G instructions} and 47.6 G cycles, 3.09 instructions per cycle, 29 \% of the cycles stalled on memory, 80 million last-level read misses, 34 million data TLB walks. That is 1,310 instructions and 425 cycles per line of the export. By compile unit (the symbol; inlined frames belong to it):}

