\p{The candidate's loader thread on Mathlib, from a profile of the same kind as section 2.3 (two profiled passes, 42,106 samples): 119.5 G instructions per pass (base 147 G) at 2.9 instructions per cycle, 31 \% of the cycles stalled on memory, 167 million mispredicted branches. By compile unit, share of the thread's time: the kernel 15.0 \%, \code{\verb~|Scanner.appStretch~} 14.4 \% (260 instructions and 64 cycles per line; with the other templates the scanner is 19.6 \%, it was 21.9 \%), \code{\verb~|Loader.resolvePending~} 4.9 \%, \code{\verb~|NodeCtx.writeApp~} 4.6 \%, \code{\verb~|Loader.nameStr~} 4.5 \%, \code{\verb~|ProofBlocks.WriterImpl.records~} 4.3 \% and \code{\verb~|Loader.blockStretch~} 2.7 \% (141 and 80 instructions per block record: with the sweep's dispatch a block record costs about 275 instructions where it cost about 410, and the path from segment to block is 9.6 \% of the thread's time where it was 13.6 \%), \code{\verb~|ProofBlocks.promote~} 3.9 \%, \code{\verb~|NameTable.internNum~} 3.7 \%, \code{\verb~|TermStore.touch~} 3.7 \%, \code{\verb~|Loader.exprApps~} 2.3 \% with \code{\verb~|Linker.apps~} 0.9 \% (the arrival of an \code{app} record: 80 instructions where it was 88, 3.2 \% of the time where it was 3.3 \%: this stretch pays for itself and no more). What is left is in [the second insight](ins-2B4K).}
}

\subtree{
\title{5.3 The guard: eight corpora, the executable and the JVM launcher}

\p{The guard of [the rule for a default](dec-YP0N): warm wall clock of a pass that reloads the file, 8 workers, load pipelined, a run without options; base and candidate interleaved round by round inside one quiet window per corpus, three rounds; a process makes 15 passes on reachability, 10 on Init and Std, 8 on cedar, 6 on con-leche, cslib and navier-stokes-euler and 4 on Mathlib; a cell is the mean over the rounds of the median later pass of a process (for a pass under 0.5 s: of the mean later pass). "Loader thread busy" is the wall clock of the loading thread in the pass; peak RSS is the largest value any pass line of the rounds reports.}

\table{
