\ul{
\li{\strong{The guard holds on both launchers.} The executable: the geometric mean goes down by 4.1 \%, seven corpora are 1.4 to 7.1 \% faster, and reachability, whose load is 35 ms of a pass of 570 ms, is at +0.1 \%. The JVM launcher: the geometric mean goes down by 3.8 \% and every corpus is 1.6 to 6.2 \% faster. No corpus is more than 3 \% slower in either, and every pass of every round ended ACCEPT with every unit accepted.}
\li{\strong{Against the estimate of rep-P11} (0.25 to 0.4 s direct on Mathlib, 0.1 s on cslib). Mathlib: -0.37 s in the executable, with no overlap between the rounds (base 14.44 to 14.64 s, candidate 14.12 to 14.23 s), and -0.50 s on the JVM launcher. cslib: -0.41 s in the executable as the mean of three rounds of a restless window (round by round -0.24, -0.76 and -0.22 s; the windows of section 5.2 give -0.34 s), and -0.12 s on the JVM launcher.}
\li{\strong{Where the loader thread is the pass, the pass follows the loader - until the workers are the bound.} On Init, Std, cedar and cslib the base's loader thread is busy for 89 to 95 \% of the executable's pass. The candidate's is busy 10 to 18 \% less, and the pass gets 4.5 to 7.1 \% shorter: then it waits for the workers, and the candidate's loader thread is busy for 78 to 91 \% of its pass. On Mathlib the loader thread is busy 0.98 s less and the pass is 0.37 s shorter; on navier-stokes-euler 0.48 s and 0.17 s.}
\li{\strong{CPU of the pass} goes down on seven corpora in both launchers and is the same on reachability: in the executable 110.0 -> 108.5 s on Mathlib and 42.0 -> 40.0 s on cslib.}
\li{\strong{Peak RSS} is the largest value of the three rounds. In the executable the rounds of base and candidate overlap on six corpora (Mathlib round by round: 7,603 7,653 7,522 against 7,543 7,455 7,514 MiB), Std is lower in every round (663 680 677 against 657 659 653 MiB), and con-leche is 18 MiB, 1.3 \%, higher in every round (1,349 1,347 1,342 against 1,367 1,367 1,359 MiB). A likely cause, not verified: the block writer asks its buffer for room for 16 bytes per record of a stretch before it writes the stretch, where a record takes about 6, so on a corpus of large blocks the buffer doubles one step earlier. On the JVM launcher the differences are those of the collector from round to round: con-leche 1,787 1,887 1,831 against 1,846 2,070 1,819 MiB, Mathlib 6,285 6,194 7,419 against 6,093 6,195 6,217 MiB.}
}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{6. The gates}

\p{All on the private candidate distribution, through its own launchers and with no \code{\verb~|-X~} option unless the row says so.}

\table{
\tr{\th{gate}\th{result}}
\tr{\td{the suites of the three modules on the candidate's sources}\td{\code{rlvm-export} 79 tests, 0 failures, 1 skipped (the Mathlib differential, which has a switch of its own; run with it: 1 test, 0 failures); \code{rlvm-store} 72, 0 failures, 1 skipped as in the main tree; \code{rlvm-load} 81, 0 failures, 0 skipped. New: \code{AppStretchTest} (3 tests: the number of digits in every place of an \code{app} line, stretches longer than the scanner's buffer and what ends them, ids that are not dense; every file through all reader configurations and the reference reader, with the sink taking the stretches and refusing them), the stretch modes of \code{PackedRunTest} (300 random blocks written through \code{records} by the interface default and by the writer against the single calls, compared word for word, also after promotion; corrupt stretches)}}
\tr{\td{\strong{store equality}: the differential digest of the loader's tests (outcome or exception with message and line, every word of the export region, every block row, every word of every decoded block, every name, the structural digest of every unit), candidate against base}\td{\strong{IDENTICAL in 25 of 25 configurations}: one thread on 17,158 small files (the 230 published tests and 16,928 mutants), the 263 arena tests of the complete set below 100 MB, 847 prelude mutants, Init, Std, the Cedar slice, reachability, cedar, con-leche, navier-stokes-euler, cslib, Mathlib; 3 scanner threads with chunks of 256 bytes and 2 with 3,000 bytes on the three lists of small files; 2 and 3 scanner threads with chunks of 64 KiB, 1 MiB and 4 MiB on the corpora (71.8 to 77.1 million records through packed runs); the strict policy with one thread and with scanner threads on the small lists. Every configuration also equals the base's one-thread digest of the same list. Strict policy on the eight corpora: identical to the base and to the practical digest, nothing declined}}
\tr{\td{the gate of the default configuration through the executable (\code{\verb~|scripts/gate.sh --defaults --corpus all --hostile --native~})}\td{PASS: 230 of 230 tests correct, none declined; 17,775 mutants: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0, agree 15,739, declined 2,034, 2 runs ended by the 60 s limit (below); the differential self-test caught; hostile suite 1,196 rows: agree 1,124, 68 tolerated accepts of kind (d), 0 wrong accept, 0 wrong reject, 4 declined}}
