\p{No wrong accept and no wrong reject against the official checker was seen in the base or in the candidate.}
}

\subtree{
\title{7. Verdict}

\p{\strong{GO for the default configuration.} The reasons, in the order of [the rule for a default](dec-YP0N):}

\ul{
\li{\strong{It is a cost-only change.} The store the loader builds is the base's store word for word in every reader configuration the loader's tests know and under both policies, and the engines count the same ticks, records and declines on all eight corpora (section 6). Nothing a worker reads is different, so no verdict can be.}
\li{\strong{Every gate passed with the release's counts}, through the executable and through the jars: 230 tests, 17,775 mutants with SOUNDNESS 0 and COMPLETENESS 0, the hostile suite with 0 wrong accept and 0 wrong reject; the invariance suite has no schedule difference; the strict policy accepts all eight corpora with nothing declined. The two mutant runs that ran into the gate's time limit do so under the host's load in the base as in the candidate, and both give the official verdict when run alone.}
\li{\strong{The guard holds on the executable and on the JVM launcher} (section 5.3): geometric mean -4.1 \% and -3.8 \%, the worst corpus +0.1 \% and -1.6 \%, three interleaved rounds each. Mathlib in the executable: 14.53 -> 14.16 s.}
\li{\strong{The price} is source: about 850 added lines in three modules, 200 of them tests - loops that do for the common case what the record-by-record paths do. They are tied to those paths by interface defaults that the tests run against them, and by the digest; whoever changes what a record-by-record path does must change its stretch, and the digest configurations of section 6 are the test that says so. Peak RSS is 1.3 \% higher on con-leche in the executable and not higher on any other corpus.}
}

\p{What the verdict rests on and does not cover: the base is the main tree of 05:23 UTC, whose three modules were unchanged when the work ended; the times are differences of interleaved rounds on a host that was busy, on aarch64; the patches were not measured together with the force-inline list of the machine that entered the main tree during the work (section 10). The integrator's own guard on the merged tree is the measurement that counts.}
}

\subtree{
\title{8. The patches, and what an integrator must know}

\ul{
\li{Three unified diffs against the repository root, one per module, to be applied together: \code{rlvm-export} (\code{Scanner}, \code{Mem}, \code{RecordOut}, \code{Linker}, \code{IdSpace}, \code{ExportSink}; the tests \code{AppStretchTest}, \code{StructSink} and \code{T}; the README), \code{rlvm-store} (\code{ProofBlocks}; the test \code{PackedRunTest}; the README), \code{rlvm-load} (\code{Loader}, \code{LoadTarget}, \code{StoreTarget}; the README). They apply to the main tree as it was when the work ended without a failed hunk, and applied to the base they give the candidate's sources file for file. \code{rlvm-load} needs the other two: it implements \code{\verb~|ExportSink.exprApps~} and calls \code{\verb~|ProofBlocks.Writer.records~}.}
\li{No build script, no option and no default changed. The force-inline list of the machine (\src{rlvm-machine/h10/force-inline.txt}, [the first lever of this wave](rep-OPT-A)) entered the main tree while this work ran; it names eight methods of \code{rlvm-store} (\code{\verb~|Terms.a~}, \code{b}, \code{kind}, \code{fvMask}, \code{hasLevelParam}, \code{\verb~|ProofBlocks.rd~}, \code{\verb~|ProofBlocks.localRef~}, \code{\verb~|DeclTable.ctorInduct~}). The patches rename, split or remove none of them: of these classes they touch only \code{ProofBlocks}, and there only its writer.}
\li{The switch of \code{\verb~|Loader.sweep~} keeps its four cases for APP, LAM, PI and LET block records although the stretch in front of it now takes every such record: they cannot be reached any more and can go in a follow-up; they were left so that the gated code is the code of the patch.}
\li{The range tests of the stretch loops rely on the node kinds APP, LAM, PI, LET being consecutive numbers; \code{ProofBlocks} and \code{Loader} assert it when they are initialised.}
\li{The READMEs of the three modules got one paragraph each for the new optional interfaces, with the marker of this report.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{9. What was tried and not kept, and what was not done}

\ul{
\li{\strong{A force-inline list for the reader and the loader} (25 methods, \code{\verb~|-H:PriorityForceInline~}): -9 \% on the load of Init and -1 to -6 \% on Mathlib, less than the source change, and the option takes one value, so the list would have to be merged into the machine's in the build. Not kept; the source change does not depend on the build.}
\li{\strong{The first two versions of the block writer's loop} (section 3, items 2 and 3): fewer instructions in the source; more instructions, or more mispredictions, in the image.}
\li{\strong{Not done, with the measurement that speaks for or against each.} A loop of their own for \code{lam} and \code{forallE} lines (13 \% of the lines; their numbers are still calls: 7.6 \% of the candidate's instructions on Init). Breaking the scanner's chain of dependent loads (section 5.2: 64 cycles per line at 4 instructions per cycle). A stretch for shared nodes: about four call levels per node, 2 \% of the instructions, and the time of a shared node is its children's cache misses. Comparing the id of a line with the expected text instead of converting it: one conversion in three. Parsing the mapped file in place: the copy is 2.4 \% of the thread.}
\li{\strong{Not attacked: memory.} The kernel's 13 to 15 \% (fresh pages; the image has no option for huge pages, and the candidates the lever named do not apply: the export region, the location table and the name table are sized from the file length and do not grow on Mathlib), the location table (5 \%), promotion (10 \%), the name table (8 \%), the children of shared nodes (12 \%).}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{10. What was not measured}

\ul{
\li{Anything on x86-64; anything with Oracle GraalVM; a quiet host (section 1): the absolute times are those of a busy host, the differences are from interleaved rounds.}
\li{The patches together with the force-inline list of the machine (section 8): base and candidate were both built from the sources of 05:23 UTC, without the list. The list changes the workers' code and, in the loader thread, one reader of \code{ProofBlocks} that promotion uses (\code{rd}); the loops of the patches call nothing that it names.}
\li{The scanner threads' own cost: with scanner threads the tapes replay record by record as before; the default configuration has none.}
\li{The first, cold pass of a process as a number of its own: the guard is the warm pass.}
\li{Which of the four changes gives how much in the pass: only two candidates' loads were counted against each other (section 5.1).}
\li{The rule for scanner threads ([the settings of a plain run](dec-EGMG)) with the faster loader thread.}
}
}
